> Keep in mind that ANY project relying on input IDs breaks with this change. Which has always been the main way to differentiate devices without creating an InputMap entry for each separate device.

I'm a bit confused now. Before the device ID change keyboards and mice had id of 0, which doesn't allow to differentiate them from other devices via the ids alone. And this change shouldn't affect InputMap, since InputMap doesn't allow the developer to specify the device ID for keyboard and mouse, and if keyboard or mouse events with id of 0 get added to InputMap, the ids are automatically adjusted to the new ones. 😅
@NancokPS2
